[2026-09-20 10:43:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 030] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-20 10:43:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 030]   step_07: decisive comet test -- Warsaw Catalogue original barycentric orbits.
[2026-09-20 10:43:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 030]   Data: J/A+A/567/A126 tablec.dat (Krolikowska 2014) -- original barycentric
[2026-09-20 10:43:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 030]   orbital elements at 250 AU inbound for 128 near-parabolic comets, with
[2026-09-20 10:43:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 030]   formal uncertainties propagated through full dynamical swarms. This is the
[2026-09-20 10:43:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 030]   proper Oort-spike dataset: comets whose aphelia have *not* yet been
[2026-09-20 10:43:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 030]   perturbed into the observable region, so their aphelion directions trace
[2026-09-20 10:43:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 030]   where the Oort cloud material actually sits.
[2026-09-20 10:43:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 030]   TEP discriminator: if a proper-time field boundary exists near the
[2026-09-20 10:43:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 030]   confined-TNO axis (lam~34 deg, beta~-13 deg ecliptic), comets arriving
[2026-09-20 10:43:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 030]   from that direction crossed the boundary -- their aphelia may show an
[2026-09-20 10:43:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 030]   excess along the axis *beyond* what the galactic tide predicts. The
[2026-09-20 10:43:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 030]   galactic tide alone predicts aphelion avoidance of the galactic equator
[2026-09-20 10:43:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 030]   (|b| structure) but is axisymmetric about the galactic pole -- it cannot
[2026-09-20 10:43:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 030]   produce a concentration toward one specific ecliptic direction.
[2026-09-20 10:43:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 030]   Tests:
[2026-09-20 10:43:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 030]   W1  isotropy of aphelion unit vectors (Rayleigh, 3D)
[2026-09-20 10:43:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 030]   W2  galactic-latitude structure vs uniform and vs tide prediction
[2026-09-20 10:43:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 030]   W3  angle between mean aphelion direction and the TNO cluster axis,
[2026-09-20 10:43:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 030]   with bootstrap direction uncertainty and tide-aware null
[2026-09-20 10:43:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 030]   W4  direct excess: fraction of aphelia within 60 deg of the TNO axis
[2026-09-20 10:43:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 030]   vs Monte Carlo nulls (uniform, and galactic-tide-weighted)
[2026-09-20 10:43:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 030]   W5  ecliptic-plane direction test on dynamically-new subset
